WEBVTT

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.160
<i>It's been a long time since we've used this room.</i>

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.340
This divination cannot be allowed the slightest error.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.360
We have to make sure everything's perfect.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.060
Let's go, Tama-chan.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.800
<i>Right, Miss.</i>

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.310
<i>Elim An Karid Visad Am Wel.</i>

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:30.230
<b>The Treasure
of the Shikimori</b>

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:40.900
The direct cause of Yuuma-kun being raised in this house was the incident where the treasure of the Shikimori went berserk.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.080
Suu-chan, I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.270
Natsune!

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.550
Natsune-chan...

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:53.550
Wait, please.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.000
The responsibility for this lies with me as the next master of the Shikimori house.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.620
If you do that, you'll...

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.420
<i>Di Latil Amalest!</i>

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.440
Suzuri-san, you can see how this is going to end.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.460
Natsune!

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.090
Natsune!

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.950
Suzuri-san...

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.120
Seal the treasure here...

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.780
Please.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:14.010
It never became public, but rumors spread that magic had killed someone,

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.200
and magic began to be viewed as something dangerous.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.130
It was then that Yuuma-kun's own incident occurred.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.280
I see...

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.850
Just using magic made him out to be a bad guy.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.330
Even though Yuuma wasn't the one who hurt someone.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.130
We swore that this must never happen again,

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:39.410
and sealed the treasure as Natsune asked.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.340
The problem was the place and method.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.840
The treasure possesses vast power.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.490
There was a need to watch over it at all times.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:59.210
We sealed the treasure in a corner of the vast forest owned by the Shikimori,

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:05.750
the Shiki Forest, and surrounded it with many powerful barriers.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.020
Then we created a school beside it.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:16.680
I would stay at the school at all times to watch over the treasure.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.910
But that task...

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:27.570
...was far too much for me with Yuuma-kun at my side.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:32.680
So I entrusted him to Otoha.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:37.020
Suzuri-chan and I have been good friends forever.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.260
There were two reasons Mizuhosaka Academy was founded.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.570
The first was to raise up wonderful mages like yourself,

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.090
and the second was to watch over the treasure.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.430
I see...

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.470
Does Yuuma-kun...?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:06:02.000
When I said good-bye to him, I sealed his memories of my name and face.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:13.410
At the time I thought of it as a punishment for my failure to save Natsune.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:19.900
But now I don't know if that was truly the right decision.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.520
Huh?  A visitor?

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.100
Who is it?

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.040
<i>Package.</i>

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.780
At this hour?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.170
I'm the one who asked for it.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.510
You did, Suzuri-chan?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.470
Yes, my magic briefcase...

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.320
Briefcase?

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.460
Thank you.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.790
Wow, I want one, too!

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.310
It's full of rare magical items!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.870
I'm going to use this to reconnect Sumomo-chan's psyche and body.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.240
While I'm healing her, I want you guys...

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.080
...to restrain Ibuki-san.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:17.620
It will take three days to completely return her to normal.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:22.810
During that time Ibuki-san may go after the treasure again.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.190
If that happens, I'll pound her flat.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.320
She's a good girl.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.280
But she's just not thinking right now.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:38.310
Natsune-neesama...

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.370
Just a bit more.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.670
Just a bit more and...

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.410
If she's going to act, it will probably be tomorrow.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:53.060
You need to rest until then-

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.220
N-No, Sumomo-chan!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:00.450
I'll bake you an apple pie, so come back!

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.100
Even though she's back in her room...

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.520
We have to act fast.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:14.460
Kamisaka-san, if you see Yuuma-kun,

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:17.290
give him this.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.430
What is it?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.930
Something Natsune left behind.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:25.030
If he uses it he should be able to control his magic to a degree.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.210
OK, take care of Yuuma for me.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.660
Don't attack him while he's asleep.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:34.310
Don't worry!

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.370
Night, Hachi!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.480
Yu-u-ma!

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.980
The obstruction's gone home!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.950
What?  You're asleep already?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.400
Goodnight, Yuuma...

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.010
Sumomo...

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.990
<i>Al Amdald Ri Elis.</i>

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:09.950
<i>Viva Lida Ledem Lune Vide.</i>

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:16.400
<i>Li Astie Astie Li Astie Astie...</i>

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.700
Sumomo-chan...

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.460
Brother, where are you?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.950
Brother?

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.510
Here, Saya.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.010
Brother!

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.390
Look at this.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.360
This is...

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.690
A rift has opened in the barrier.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:52.350
The fight yesterday was probably the cause.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.040
It's even affected areas this far out?

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:59.490
We're a ways from where they fought yesterday.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.020
What?

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.600
It's not where the fight took place yesterday?

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.440
You got lost again, didn't you?

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.170
That doesn't matter.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.240
We can finally enter the Shiki Forest.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.880
This disaster is to our benefit.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.530
We must report this to Ibuki-sama immediately.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.420
Are you really going to report it?

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.310
What are you trying to say?

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:28.050
If Ibuki-sama gets her hands on the treasure,
there will be a fight as they attempt to regain it.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:32.290
Even so, we must obey her.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.740
Brother...

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:35.680
Enough!

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.200
Ibuki-sama's mansion is over there.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.080
Wake up!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.550
Today's a holiday, so let's go play somewhere.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.460
It's nice outside.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:51.980
So it is.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.010
<i>Li Astim Astim.</i>

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.130
<i>Li Astim Astim.</i>

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.350
<i>Li Astim Astim.</i>

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.750
<i>Li Astim Astim...</i>

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.880
Good luck, Sumomo-chan, Suzuri-chan...

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.560
This is...

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.510
It's cold!

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.630
Soprano, has there been any response to your detection magic?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.120
<i>Nothing yet.</i>

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.340
But she's going to act soon, I'm sure of it.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.820
Haruhi, I'm coming in.

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:50.270
Come in.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.320
Are you ready?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.580
Yes, I'm ready.

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.790
Takamine-senpai?

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:14.700
Kamisaka-san, Hiiragi-san...  There's something I have to tell you...

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.460
Senpai!

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:45.650
I had been fasting to perform an extremely important divination.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:49.320
<i>She hadn't eaten a thing since yesterday!</i>

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:53.050
What was it you had to divine that was so important?

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.710
The future of this school.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:00.170
You're going to stop Ibuki-san, aren't you?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.880
How do you know that?

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:05.530
Then you know about the treasure, too?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:11.330
I remember well the time when
Natsune-neesama was still alive.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:17.920
I was still a child at the time, but I played with young Ibuki-san often.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:24.770
At the time, she was a very kind-hearted open girl who was very attached to her sister.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:30.510
But when she learned the truth of her sister's death,

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:40.270
and that the treasure had already been sealed away, she changed.

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.400
Why?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:47.670
The treasure of the Shikimori proves its owner to be the head of the Shikimori family.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:49.730
Ibuki-san has always thought...

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:55.590
...since she was a child that if she became the head of the Shikimori the treasure would be hers.

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:57.590
But the treasure...

00:13:57.590 --> 00:14:03.190
It was given to Minagi-sensei, who has no connection to the Shikimori family.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.640
Ibuki-san is probably planning to recover it for herself,

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:12.000
as the next head of the family, by whatever means necessary.

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.030
The barrier fell?

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.210
Good work finding it.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.810
Good work, Shinya!  Saya!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:21.230
Ma'am.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:26.200
The treasure of the Shikimori has dwelt in the hands of the head of the Shikimori for generations.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:33.810
I promised Natsune-neesama that I would someday inherit it if I became the head of the family.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.580
The time to fulfill that promise has finally come.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:38.390
Let us go!

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:41.160
Uhm, Ibuki-sama?

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.900
What is it, Saya?

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:48.380
I feel unwell.  May I rest for a while?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:52.110
I think I'll be ready after a short rest.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.370
Very well.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.960
Follow us as soon as possible.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:57.550
Yes...

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:13.010
Actually, around February, Ibuki-san snuck into the school to try and find the treasure.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.150
Huh?!

00:15:14.150 --> 00:15:15.810
Is that true?

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:23.430
I was able to detect this ahead of time,
and waited for her inside the school to stop her.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.980
Then you got rid of her, right?

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.170
I couldn't.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:30.030
<i>Yep.</i>

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:33.790
Leave.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.950
I won't let anyone get in my way, no matter who they are!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.480
Bisaim!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:44.750
I'll show mercy to an old friend.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.830
Leave before you get hurt.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.120
I have no choice.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.790
I'll use my trump card.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:53.970
Tama-chan!

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>Aye-aye, sir!</i>

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.290
No way...

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.880
<i>Ibuki-sama, we must evacuate.</i>

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.500
<i>Kaboom!</i>

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:15.200
That was you, Senpai?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.040
Unfortunately...

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.620
It wasn't a gas explosion!

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:25.560
<i>Haruhi, someone's gone inside the barrier.</i>

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:32.990
Somebody has placed detection magic here.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.020
Don't worry about it.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:37.140
There's nothing they can do.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.990
It's Ibuki-san, right?

00:16:44.990 --> 00:16:46.140
Yes.

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:51.520
My divination showed that if she acquires the treasure, something bad will happen.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.350
Let's go.

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:56.470
We must stop her, no matter what.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.020
OK!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:02.540
Kamisaka-san, you have something else you must do.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.160
Find Yuuma-san.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.210
Why Yuuma-kun?

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.010
Yuuma-san is our trump card.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:16.610
When we reach the end of this, his presence will be very important.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:20.520
Kamisaka-san, if you see Yuuma-kun,

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.110
give him this.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.730
Very well.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.320
That was fun, huh, Yuuma?

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.160
Yuuma!

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.570
Wh-What?

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:57.000
Jeez... You're on a date with such a beautiful girl.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.490
If you can't look like you're at least enjoying it a bit, I'll smack you.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.920
Nothing to say?

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.240
Hey!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.290
Hey!  You perverted kid, come back!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:16.040
Jeez... Yuuma, let's go!

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:18.960
Yuuma?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:23.500
Yeah, I'm getting it.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.080
Hello?

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.360
K-Kamisaka-san?!

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.630
Wh-What's up?

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.180
You're calling me...

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:37.410
Are you going to ask me out on a d-date?

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:39.350
MANGA:  Shounen Positive!

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:41.550
Do you know where Yuuma-kun is?

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:46.360
I kinda figured that was it...

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.550
Did you get in a fight with him or something?

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:51.160
No, that's not it.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.040
But why?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:58.360
He was all alone in the park in the rain yesterday.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:03.900
He didn't look like he was going home, so I had him stay at Jun's place.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.710
Then is he still there?

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:13.120
Nah, Jun called me a while to say that he was gonna drag him somewhere whether he liked it or not.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:14.500
Where?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.350
Uhm... I think he was saying something about the aquarium...

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:23.260
Yeah, he was with me until a second ago.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.310
But we got separated.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.800
And it looks like his cellphone is off.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:29.050
I can't get a hold of him.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.440
I'll find him somehow.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.490
Let's meet up later, Haruhi-chan.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:39.520
Soprano, hurry to the aquarium!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:41.430
<i>Very good, Haruhi.</i>

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:55.560
SIGN:  Sakura Aquarium

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.660
What am I doing in a place like this?

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.600
What happened after that?

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:17.470
If anything happened to Sumomo, what should I do?

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:26.470
Haruhi...

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:32.310
What should I do?

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:43.080
It looks like the barrier isn't broken yet.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.840
What do you think, Senpai?

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:48.150
Can you repair it?

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:53.300
There are only a few mages in the world capable of creating a barrier this powerful.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:59.000
Even if it isn't totally broken, it's not something that can be easily repaired.

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:06.440
<i>Any mage with a reasonable amount of power could break a mostly-broken barrier though.</i>

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:07.750
I see...

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:11.980
We have to stop them from going in ourselves, huh?

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.550
Yeah, that's about it.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:18.850
Anyway, what's Shikimori Ibuki doing?

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:22.360
She noticed this place a long time ago, right?

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:27.030
Why did we get here first?

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:30.030
<i>Anri-sama, over there!</i>

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:42.270
Someone got here first...

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.520
Wh-What the hell happened to you?

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:46.870
You're covered in leaves...

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.070
Shut up!

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.580
We just kind of got lost!

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.530
I'm terribly sorry, Ibuki-sama.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:58.560
But we won't get lost from here.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:00.710
We're going through.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:03.900
Sorry, this area is off-limits.

00:23:55.080 --> 00:24:25.040
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.110
This is Kamisaka Haruhi!

00:23:57.110 --> 00:24:01.430
This is the last time I'll be doing a preview on TV.

00:24:01.430 --> 00:24:03.020
Oosugi-san in Kyoto,

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:04.510
Minawa-san in Tokyo!

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:06.490
Thanks for watching every week!

00:24:06.490 --> 00:24:09.900
Saitou-san in Chiba, you shouldn't knock something until you've tried it.

00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:12.020
Watch once in a while!

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.520
Everybody who saw the show, and everybody who couldn't,

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:16.450
